firms modemrail<100mV before release. Independent MODEM_RESET GPIO7/physical12 and independent hardware qualified modemRUN remain unchanged. A new .40/.15 Type7 pole at72.6,9.3 is the only under-U800 OFF hole; receiver68.8,33.1 is ordinary .45/.20, and four routed .40/.15 ordinary transition holes stay outside all primary bodies. Exact factory profile required for each hole, not generic .20drill fabrication. All original power/ground/source roles are separately verified after native refill.  Physical43/GPIO38 remains FAULTinput; physical24/GPIO18 remainsunused due documentedtypical high glitch. PreserveUART0 recovery49/50 and the exact clock/DIO/BUSY pins17/21/22. Radio uses lowest useful GPIO drive, initial1MHz SPI, qualified PG and independent hardware OE/RUN gating. GPIO21/physical27 requests internalUSB only after initializationLOW; physical36 observes externalVBUS. No undocumentedM2UART. Physical14/GPIO9ADC1_CH8 remains analog current observation withoutdigitaldrive orpull. Recovery holds modemOFF>=5s, confirmsrail<100mV before restart; blankMCU autostart remainshardware-backed. New exact .40/.15 Type7 U800 escape holes require both faces planar capped with no proud copper and the literal factory mask/flatness profile; all other transition holes use explicit ordinary tenting and no fill/cap. Low-rate reset/RXEN F/In2/In3/B routes guard actual current571 XTAL three-height return field and all high-current power sheets. A deliberate4.6223mm F0.4 AON source bridge joins Fentry73.5,14.6 through explicitly qualifiedType7pole73.525,14.575 and enlarged ordinary75.49,18.4 source pole to restore physical46/C805 input; exact source/return/125C sensitivity is separately proved. Actual inherited UART/DIO reference fringe deltas remain enumerated without a blanket equality claim. This is layout/source evidence, not powered transient or waveform proof. Modem current monitor: U986 has no separateFLT; Physical40/GPIO35 is explicitly NC after removing the obsolete constantLOW current-status connection. U749 output2 is also explicitly NC while its input6 remains GND. Firmware must not assign GPIO35 to the retired OOB_CURRENT_OK function or interpret that obsolete signal as a current fault. MAIN_OK, MODEM_PG, coarsecurrentADC, actualrailADC and independentSTOP/RESET remain unchanged. GPIO9 ADC1CH8 uses combinedILM guarded1M/100k pluslocal100nC989. Configure calibratedATTEN0, WiFiOFF duringsampling, noGPIOdrive/pulls; >=150ms settle afterisolationenable/railstartup, discardfirstconversion andaverage. Report coarsecalibratedloadbins with±5mV25C primaryADC plusgain/leakage/temperatureuncertainty, neverzero=currentOFF. ActualPG andrailADC plusindependentSTOP/RESETremainrecoveryauthority. I2C1446 source escape: SDA now physical19/GPIO14, former physical41/GPIO36 NC; SCL remains physical42/GPIO37. GPIO14 Table2-1 AtReset field blank, AfterReset IE; no internal-pull claim. Initialize SDA/SCL high latch before output enable, input/output open-drain through GPIO matrix, external2.49k pulls only,100kHz; bounded bus errors/stale state UNKNOWN. Every ADC/control/recovery pin and GPIO21 REQUEST reset correction are retained. One sealed Type7 own-U800 source pole and eleven ordinary tented public150um jobs require explicit manufacturer acceptance; first-board rise-time and stuck-bus/recovery checks required. Local observer1498: physical38/GPIO33 and physical39/GPIO34 are now NC; MAIN_OK/MODEM_PG status is read from local U840 I2C0x41 P0/P1 via retained unidirectional U749 outputs. No recovery/control GPIO reassignment. Bus failure reportsUNKNOWN; actualrail/currentADC and STOP/RESET remain independent." (id 5) (at 246.38 154.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left) hide)) (property "Manufacturer" "Espressif" (id 6) (at 246.38 154.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left) hide)) (property "MPN" "ESP32-S3FN8" (id 7) (at 246.38 154.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left) hide)) (pin "1" (uuid 28f914ce-cddf-494c-9e2e-60